doctype html
html lang=I18n.locale
  head
    meta charset="utf-8"
    = favicon_link_tag asset_path('favicon.ico')
    title
      = content_for?(:title) ? yield(:title) : MetaHelper::SITE_NAME

    meta[name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"]
    = render 'shared/meta'
    / No csrf_meta_tags here on purpose. Nothing on the public theme makes a non-GET request —
    / the only form is the GET search — and the masked token in that tag changes on every
    / response, which made the ETag change on every response too. Without it, a reader who
    / comes back to a page they have already read gets a 304 with no body instead of the whole
    / page again. Rails' form helpers carry their own token in a hidden field, so a form added
    / here later still works; only a hand-written fetch() would need the tag back.
    = csp_meta_tag
    / The four faces are self-hosted (theme/_fonts.scss) — no runtime request to
    / Google Fonts. Preload only the slices the first paint actually needs.
    - theme_preloaded_faces.each do |face|
      link rel="preload" href=asset_path("#{face}.woff2") as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin=""
    = stylesheet_link_tag 'theme', media: 'all'
    = javascript_include_tag 'theme', defer: true

  body.rc-site
    a.rc-skip href="#main"= t('global.skip_to_content')
    = render NavComponent.new
    = render 'shared/theme_flash'
    main#main.rc-main.page-in tabindex="-1"
      = yield
    = render FooterComponent.new
    = render 'shared/quote_card'
